// A `comptime_assert` whose condition is a CONCRETE false must fail the
// compile from INSIDE a function body, not only at module level.
//
// It used to be inert here: `evaluate_comptime_assert` returned early whenever
// `!ctx.is_executing`, and a function body is VALIDATED rather than executed —
// so the assertion was reduced to a type check. A `test("…", { … })` body is a
// function body too, which made all 1559 `comptime_assert` calls under `tests/`
// verify nothing (issues/fixed/comptime-assert-never-fires-inside-a-function-body.md).
check_me :: (fn() -> unit)({
  comptime_assert((2 + 2) == 5);
});
main :: (fn() -> unit)({
  check_me();
});
export(main);
